          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The Burnside ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(G)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is the analogue of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            in the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
            over a field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            Elements of the Burnside ring are thus formal differences of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            (with respect to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a contravariant functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtext FinGrp
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %mtext AbRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \text{FinGrp} \xrightarrow{A} \text{AbRing}
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For
            %em any
            group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %em
              Burnside
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^G
            of finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representations"} permutation representations
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^G
            and the multiplication operation descended from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet^G
          %p
            (In fact the Burnside rig
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(G)
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+ring"} exponential ring
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed structure
            of the topos. )
          %p
            The
            %em Burnside ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(G)
            is then the (additive)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            of the Burnside rig,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(G) = \mathbb{Z} \otimes_{\mathbb{N}} B(G)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
            is the coproduct of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(G)
            in the category of commutative rigs, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℕ
                  %mo −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \otimes_{\mathbb{N}} -
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to the forgetful functor from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            to commutative rigs.)
          %p
            More generally, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+category"} distributive category
            determines a Burnside rig (
            %a{:href => "#Schanuel91"}> Schanuel91
            ).
          %p
            Explicitly, the Burnside ring can be seen to be the free abelian group on the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G / H_1 , G / H_2, \ldots, G / H_t
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{1}, \ldots, H_{t}
            are representatives of the distinct conjugacy classes of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BurnsideMultiplicities"}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#span_by_the_coset_spaces_
            Span by the coset spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
          %p
            Since every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of the basic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+spaces"} coset spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \hookrightarrow G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H_2
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_2
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugate
            to each other, the Burnside ring is spanned, as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            by the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G/H]
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            ranging over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
            of subgroups.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi H
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  A(G)
                  \\;\simeq_{\mathbb{Z}}\;
                  \\underset{[H \subset G]}{\oplus}
                  [G/H]
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representations"} permutation representations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[G/H]
            corresponding to these generators are precisely the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induced+representations+of+trivial+representations"} induced representations of trivial representations
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ind
                      %mi H
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[G/H] \simeq ind_H^G(\mathbf{1})
          %h3#InTermsOfTheTableOfMarks In terms of the table of marks
          %p
            We discuss how the product in the Burnside ring is encoded in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+of+marks"} table of marks
            of the given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
          #BurnsideMultiplicities.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Burnside multiplicities)
            %p
              Given a choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linear order
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugacy+classes"} conjugacy classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              (for instance as in
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "table+of+marks#LinearOrderOnConjugacyClassesOfSubgroups"} this Lemma
              %em structure constants
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %em Burnside multiplicities
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                      %mi ℓ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    n_{i j}^\ell \;\in\; \mathbb{N}
            %p
              uniquely defined by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
            #eq:BurnsideStructureConstants.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi ℓ
                    %msubsup
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                      %mi ℓ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi ℓ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [G/H_i] \times [G/H_j]
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underset{ \ell }{\sum}
                    n_{i j}^\ell [G/H_\ell]
                    \\,.
          #BurnsideProductInTermsOfTableOfMarks.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
                product in terms of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+of+marks"} table of marks
            %p
              The Burnside ring structure constants
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi n
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                        %mi ℓ
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left( n_{i j}^\ell\right)
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BurnsideMultiplicities"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+of+marks"} table of marks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              and its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+matrix"} inverse matrix
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{-1}
              (which exists by
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "table+of+marks#TableOfMarksIsInvertibleUpperTriangular"} this Prop.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                      %mi l
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi m
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi t
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi m
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mi m
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mi l
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    n_{i j}^l
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underset{1 \leq m \leq t}{\sum}
                    M_{i m} \cdot M_{j m}
                    \\cdot
                    (M^{-1})_{m l}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              is the dimension of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ×
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \times t
              matrix.
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            see at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/table+of+marks"} table of marks
            %a{:href => "table+of+marks#BurnsideProductInTermsOfTableOfMarks"} this Prop.
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#action_on_products Action on products
          %p
            Given two finite groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            we have a natural linear map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mi H
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{G,H} : A(G) \otimes A(H) \to A(G \times H)
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a finite
            = succeed "-set" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a finite
            = succeed "-set," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \times T
            is naturally a finite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \times H
            set, and we may define
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo ×
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{G,H}( [S] \otimes [T]) = [S \times T]
          %p
            One can check that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            makes the Burnside ring functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi FinVect
                    %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A : FinSet^G \to FinVect^G
            into a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FinVect
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinVect
            stands for the category of finite-dimensional vector spaces. Indeed
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %span.newWikiWord
              symmetric monoidal functor
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/symmetric"} ?
            lax monoidal functor.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{G,H}
            is typically
            %em not
            an isomorphism, but:
          #LaxatorIsIsomorphism.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If the orders of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              are relatively prime, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mi H
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{G,H} : A(G) \otimes A(H) \to A(G \times H)
              is an isomorphism.
          %p
            A proof can be found
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/2524089/burnside-ring-of-the-direct-product"} on Math Stackexchange
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            are finite groups of relatively prime order, every subgroup of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \times H
            is a product of a subgroup of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and a subgroup of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
