            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(G) \otimes A(H)
            is 4-dimensional, but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ×
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(G \times H)
            is 5-dimensional.
          %h3#AsTheEquivariantStableCohomotopyOfThePoint As the equivariant stable cohomotopy of the point
          #BurnsideRingIsEquivariantStableCohomotopyOfPoint.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring+is+equivariant+stable+cohomotopy+of+the+point"}> Burnside ring is equivariant stable cohomotopy of the point
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(G)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+cohomotopy"} equivariant stable cohomotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}_G(\ast)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
              in degree 0.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A(G) \overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{S}_G(\ast)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is originally due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Segal71"} Segal 71
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Segal78"} Segal 78, p. 2
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#tomDieck79"} tom Dieck 79, theorem 7.6.7, 8.5.1
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Lueck05"} Lück 05, theorem 1.13
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#tomDieckPetrie78"} tom Dieck-Petrie 78
          %p
            From a broader perspective, this statement is a special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tom+Dieck+splitting"} tom Dieck splitting
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+suspension+spectra"} equivariant suspension spectra
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Schwede15"} Schwede 15, theorem 6.14
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "tom+Dieck+splitting#OfFixedPointSpectraOfEquivariantSuspensionSpectra"} there
